WEBVTT

00:00:03.100 --> 00:00:06.544
A seed tag is the proof of what went in the ground.

00:00:06.544 --> 00:00:12.150
Photograph the tag, open the photo, tap the info button, and mark it as a seed tag.

00:00:12.851 --> 00:00:16.065
Now attach the tag to the area it was used on.

00:00:16.065 --> 00:00:19.489
Open the drawing, choose Edit, then Attach Photo.

00:00:19.489 --> 00:00:22.144
Your tag photos have their own filter.

00:00:22.144 --> 00:00:24.031
Pick the tag, and tap Done.

00:00:24.741 --> 00:00:28.377
Then tap the label under the photo to make it a material tag.

00:00:28.377 --> 00:00:32.371
Say which product it belongs to, and how many tags are in the shot.

00:00:33.075 --> 00:00:35.165
Save the entry.

00:00:36.041 --> 00:00:40.188
One thing is left, the bag weight. It is set once per project.

00:00:40.188 --> 00:00:47.011
In Settings, open Bag weights, name the mix, then enter the pounds per bag and the rate from the spec.

00:00:47.719 --> 00:00:51.276
Open the tag photo again, and the ledger has done the math.

00:00:51.276 --> 00:00:55.978
The tags in the photo, times the bag weight, less what went down on this area.

00:00:55.978 --> 00:00:58.209
What is left carries to the next one.

00:00:58.911 --> 00:01:05.801
The tracker log shows the tags beside the pounds, and the seeding record exports with the tag photos attached.
